Bruce Ellison began as a mime and voice-over for television, as well as in musical comedies in Indiana, USA.  In 1986, after attending the Marcel Marceau International Mime School in Paris, Bruce founds the Mandragore Theatre Co. with Michel Carcan in Brussels. The troup creates the mimodrama, 'The Strange Mr. Knight', to international acclaim. Currently Bruce does voice work for radio, cinema, and children's tv programs.  He is also the singer of rock group PPZ30.

Druss Lecomte (piano) whose colourful play will remind you of the swing of Count Basie and Nat King Cole, the stride of Thomas "Fats" Waller, James P. Johnson, the humour of Erroll Garner ;

